*> variables_move.cbl -- demonstrates: WORKING-STORAGE variable
*> declarations with PIC clauses, VALUE initializers, and MOVE to copy
*> values between data items and into a fresh literal.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. VARSMOVE.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-CUSTOMER-NAME    PIC X(20) VALUE "UNKNOWN".
01  WS-ITEM-COUNT       PIC 9(4)  VALUE 0.
01  WS-BACKUP-COUNT     PIC 9(4)  VALUE 0.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    DISPLAY "INITIAL NAME: " WS-CUSTOMER-NAME.
    MOVE "SMITH" TO WS-CUSTOMER-NAME.
    DISPLAY "UPDATED NAME: " WS-CUSTOMER-NAME.

    MOVE 42 TO WS-ITEM-COUNT.
    MOVE WS-ITEM-COUNT TO WS-BACKUP-COUNT.
    DISPLAY "ITEM COUNT: " WS-ITEM-COUNT.
    DISPLAY "BACKUP COUNT: " WS-BACKUP-COUNT.
    STOP RUN.
